<div class="row">
  <br>
</div>
<div class="row">
  <% if @error_object.empty? %>
    <h2>Summary of alleles queried using fuzzy query:</h2>
    <% if ! JSON.parse(@response_from_registry).empty? %>
       <div class="well well-sm">

       <% if JSON.parse(@response_from_registry).is_a?(Array) %>

         <h3>Canonical allele identifiers for mutations based on nucleotide sequences.</h3>
         <% if @searched_type == 'p.' %>
	   <h5>The following table provides identifiers for the <strong>nucleotide</strong> changes that lead to amino-acid changes specified in the query <em>(Gene: <%= @searched_gene%> Variation: <%= @searched_variation %>)</em>. We recommend and encourage to use the identifier(s) provided in this table to identify variants in annotation systems (for example, Pathogenicity Calculator or Variant Curation Interface). </h5>
           <br>
         <% end %>

	 <%= render :partial => 'bulk_query/bulk_partial', :locals => {:input_response => @response_from_registry , :input_hgvs => @hgvs} %>
       <% end %>
       </div>
    <% end %>
    <br>
    <br>
    <% if ! JSON.parse(@response_from_registry_protein).empty? %>
     <% if @searched_type != 'c.' %>
          <div class="well well-sm">
            <h3>Amino-acid allele identifiers for mutations based on amino-acid sequences sequences.</h3>
	   <h5>The following table provides identifiers for the <strong>amino-acid</strong> changes. If there is a table <strong>above</strong> this table and has identifiers (canonical allele identifiers - CAIds) then we recommend and encourage to use them for identifying variants in annotation systems (for example, Pathogenicity Calculator or Variant Curation Interface). </h5>
           <br>
            <% if JSON.parse(@response_from_registry_protein).is_a?(Array) %>
                 <%= render :partial => 'bulk_query/bulk_partial', :locals => {:input_response => @response_from_registry_protein , :input_hgvs => @hgvs_p} %>
            <% end %>
          </div>
       <% end %>
    <% end %>
  <% else %>
     <div class="col-sm-12 bg-danger text-danger">
	<h4> An error occured while parsing the information you provided. </h4>
	<p> The following information might be helpful to understand the reason.  </p>

	<p> <b>Description of the error:</b> <%= @error_object["description"] %> </p>
	<p> <b>Explanation:</b> <%= @error_object["message"] %> </p>
     </div>
  <% end %>

    
</div>

